      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofvinton.org/history-of-vinton",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the 1940s and 1950s, Vinton’s downtown thrived with factories like the Iowa Canning Company, which hosted Sweet Corn Day each Labor Day.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofvinton.org/history-of-vinton",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Vinton’s last Chevrolet dealership closed as the town’s small factories, except Iowa Canning, shut down in the late 20th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofvinton.org/history-of-vinton",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Vinton is the county seat of Benton County and sits on the Cedar River, which flooded the city most recently in 2008.",
